{#
  Select bar — one of the site's two selection components, for picking a
  piece of DATA: a section, a calendar, an account, a rentable asset, a
  set of badges. The list is data-driven, grows with the unit, and its
  labels are long.

  The other one is partials/nav_rail.html.twig, for moving between the
  fixed sub-pages/views of one page. The rule, when a new call site
  appears (docs/module-development.md carries it too):

      fixed set, declared in code, short labels  → nav rail
      open-ended set, coming from the database   → select bar

  They share no markup and no JS. A select bar never renders chips; a
  nav rail never opens a panel. Do not add a use-case-specific parameter
  to either (no `is_section`, no `for_finance`) — a call site that seems
  to need one is using the wrong component.

  Shape: one full-width row (the <summary>) showing the field name, the
  current value and a chevron; it opens a disclosure panel anchored
  directly under the bar, holding the full list.

  The panel is a native <details>/<summary>, never a Bootstrap offcanvas
  or modal (same reason modules/groups/views/list.html.twig uses one): it
  opens, closes and announces its own state with no JavaScript at all.
  That is what preserves this component's JS-off guarantee — every item
  is rendered server-side and operable without JS, which /calendar,
  /trombinoscope and /notifications need because they are in
  Core\Offline\OfflineWhitelist. An offcanvas would silently lose it: with
  JS off the panel could never be opened at all.

  Usage:
  {% include 'partials/select_bar.html.twig' with {
      picker_id: 'section-picker',
      label: 'Section',
      items: [
          { id: 1, label: 'Louveteaux', sublabel: 'Meute', color: '#f5a623', badge: null, selected: true },
          { id: 2, label: 'Éclaireurs', sublabel: 'Troupe', color: '#4a90d9', selected: false }
      ],
      mode: 'single',
      base_url: '/chefs/staffs?section=',
      extra_query: '',
      empty_text: 'Aucune section disponible.'
  } %}

  Parameters:
  - `picker_id`  — unique per instance on a page; it is the DOM id.
  - `label`      — the field name shown as a small caption above the
                   current value ("Section", "Calendrier", "Compte").
  - `items`      — `id` and `label` required; `sublabel`, `color`,
                   `badge`, `selected` optional. Same item contract as
                   the chip picker this replaced.
  - `mode`       — 'single' (default) or 'multi'.
  - `base_url` / `extra_query` — 'single' only; the row's href is
                   `{{ base_url }}{{ item.id }}{{ extra_query }}`.
  - `empty_text` — shown instead of the control when `items` is empty.
  - `none_selected_text` — the trigger's value when nothing is selected.
  - `count_label` — plural noun for the 'multi' trigger's summary when
                   more than one item is selected ("2 badges").

  mode: 'single' — panel rows are plain
  <a href="{{ base_url }}{{ item.id }}{{ extra_query }}">, exactly as the
  chip picker's were: one selection path, and zero JS needed to select.
  `aria-current="true"` marks the selected row. A screen reader, a JS-off
  browser and a cached offline page all work.

  mode: 'multi' — rows are <button aria-pressed>, toggled by
  public/assets/js/select-bar.js, which dispatches a `select-bar:change`
  CustomEvent (detail: { selectedIds }) on the container after every
  toggle. The trigger summarises the selection rather than drawing every
  pick. This partial and its JS never persist anything themselves — the
  caller listens for the event and persists however it needs to. The
  panel stays open across toggles, which is native <details> behaviour
  and needs no code.

  Zero items renders `empty_text` and no <details> — there is nothing to
  choose from. A single item in mode 'single' renders as static text, no
  chevron and no <details>, for the same reason: navigating to the only
  option is a no-op, and nothing to choose from is not a control. Mode
  'multi' keeps its control at one item, because "assigned or not" is
  still a real choice there.

  The <summary> is the only tap target, and it takes its height from
  app.css's `pointer: coarse` block (via `.tap-target`), never from an
  inline `min-height` — design.md §7.2.
#}
{% macro row_content(item, selected) %}
    <span class="d-inline-flex align-items-center justify-content-center flex-shrink-0" style="width:1.1rem;">
        <i class="bi bi-check-lg text-primary{{ selected ? '' : ' invisible' }}" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    </span>
    {% if item.color is defined and item.color %}
        <span class="d-inline-block rounded-circle flex-shrink-0" style="width:0.6rem;height:0.6rem;background-color:{{ item.color }};"></span>
    {% endif %}
    <span class="flex-grow-1 text-start">
        <span class="d-block select-bar-row-label">{{ item.label }}</span>
        {% if item.sublabel is defined and item.sublabel %}
            <span class="d-block text-body-secondary" style="font-size:0.75rem;">{{ item.sublabel }}</span>
        {% endif %}
    </span>
    {% if item.badge is defined and item.badge %}
        <span class="badge bg-warning-subtle text-warning-emphasis flex-shrink-0">{{ item.badge }}</span>
    {% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
{% set _mode = mode|default('single') %}
{% set _selected = [] %}
{% for item in items %}
    {% if item.selected is defined and item.selected %}
        {% set _selected = _selected|merge([item]) %}
    {% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% set _none_text = none_selected_text|default('Choisir…') %}
{% if _selected|length == 0 %}
    {% set _value = _none_text %}
{% elseif _selected|length == 1 %}
    {% set _value = _selected[0].label %}
{% else %}
    {% set _value = _selected|length ~ ' ' ~ count_label|default('éléments') %}
{% endif %}
{# A colour dot on the trigger only when exactly one item is selected —
   with several picks there is no single colour to show. #}
{% set _dot = _selected|length == 1 and _selected[0].color is defined ? _selected[0].color : null %}
<div class="select-bar" id="{{ picker_id }}" data-mode="{{ _mode }}">
    {% if items|length == 0 %}
        <p class="text-body-secondary fst-italic mb-0">{{ empty_text|default('Aucun élément.') }}</p>
    {% elseif _mode != 'multi' and items|length == 1 %}
        {# Nothing to choose from is not a control (see docblock). The
           row's own detail — sublabel, badge, colour dot — still shows:
           it describes the value, it is not part of choosing one, and
           dropping it would cost a one-section unit its branch name and
           its « Non configurée » badge. #}
        <div class="select-bar-static d-flex align-items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 border rounded bg-body-tertiary">
            {% if items[0].color is defined and items[0].color %}
                <span class="d-inline-block rounded-circle flex-shrink-0" style="width:0.6rem;height:0.6rem;background-color:{{ items[0].color }};"></span>
            {% endif %}
            <span class="flex-grow-1 text-start">
                <span class="d-block text-body-secondary" style="font-size:0.75rem;">{{ label|default('') }}</span>
                <span class="d-block select-bar-value">{{ items[0].label }}</span>
                {% if items[0].sublabel is defined and items[0].sublabel %}
                    <span class="d-block text-body-secondary" style="font-size:0.75rem;">{{ items[0].sublabel }}</span>
                {% endif %}
            </span>
            {% if items[0].badge is defined and items[0].badge %}
                <span class="badge bg-warning-subtle text-warning-emphasis flex-shrink-0">{{ items[0].badge }}</span>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    {% else %}
        <details class="select-bar-details border rounded bg-body-tertiary">
            <summary class="select-bar-trigger tap-target d-flex align-items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2">
                {% if _dot %}
                    <span class="d-inline-block rounded-circle flex-shrink-0" style="width:0.6rem;height:0.6rem;background-color:{{ _dot }};"></span>
                {% endif %}
                <span class="flex-grow-1 text-start">
                    <span class="d-block text-body-secondary" style="font-size:0.75rem;">{{ label|default('') }}</span>
                    {# The two summary texts travel as data attributes so
                       select-bar.js can rebuild the trigger after a
                       toggle without inventing user-facing French of its
                       own — all wording stays server-side, in Twig. #}
                    <span class="d-block select-bar-value"
                          data-none-text="{{ _none_text }}"
                          data-count-label="{{ count_label|default('éléments') }}">{{ _value }}</span>
                </span>
                <i class="bi bi-chevron-down select-bar-chevron text-body-secondary flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </summary>
            <div class="select-bar-panel border-top">
                <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
                    {% for item in items %}
                        {% set selected = item.selected is defined and item.selected %}
                        <li class="list-group-item p-0">
                            {% if _mode == 'multi' %}
                                <button type="button"
                                        class="select-bar-item list-group-item-action d-flex align-items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 w-100 text-start border-0 bg-transparent"
                                        data-id="{{ item.id }}"
                                        data-selected="{{ selected ? 'true' : 'false' }}"
                                        aria-pressed="{{ selected ? 'true' : 'false' }}">
                                    {{ _self.row_content(item, selected) }}
                                </button>
                            {% else %}
                                <a href="{{ base_url }}{{ item.id }}{{ extra_query|default('') }}"
                                   class="select-bar-item list-group-item-action d-flex align-items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 text-decoration-none text-body"
                                   data-id="{{ item.id }}"
                                   data-selected="{{ selected ? 'true' : 'false' }}"
                                   {{ selected ? 'aria-current="true"' : '' }}>
                                    {{ _self.row_content(item, selected) }}
                                </a>
                            {% endif %}
                        </li>
                    {% endfor %}
                </ul>
            </div>
        </details>
    {% endif %}
</div>
